.TH FL-NOTIFYD 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-notifyd \- fldesktop notification server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-notifyd\fR [\fB\-\-replace\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the desktop notifications that programs send through the
\fIorg.freedesktop.Notifications\fR D-Bus interface (specification 1.2):
summary, body, icon or image, action buttons and urgency. Notifications
appear in the top right corner, stack up to five deep and disappear after
their timeout; moving the pointer over them pauses the timeout. Clicking a
notification runs its default action and closes it, the cross closes it
without an action. Critical notifications stay until they are closed.
.PP
The panel's bell button lists the notification history and switches
\fIdo not disturb\fR, which keeps everything but critical notifications from
popping up. Settings are in the Notifications page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1).
.PP
fl-notifyd is started at login through
\fI/etc/xdg/autostart/fl-notifyd.desktop\fR and can also be started by
D-Bus activation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-replace\fR
Take over from a notification server that is already running.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/notifications.ini\fR
[Notifications] DoNotDisturb, Timeout (seconds), HistorySize and Muted
(application names separated by semicolons).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBnotify-send\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
